      "body": "# Independent HQ runtime ownership repair \u2014 `.42` candidate\n\n**Draft until all eight packaging jobs and independent exact-tag audits pass.**\nThe recommended public download remains[`.40`](https://github.com/cstanislav/opentt3d/releases/tag/opentt3d-dev-20261003.40).\n`.41` stays immutable, withheld and unrecommended; no attachment is replaced.\n\nThis is a runtime-only development checkpoint with the unchanged**1,831-model**\ncatalogue and original compiler/bindings. It repairs automatic HQ LODs so independently\nowned cells do not inflate into neighbours or fill real openings. CPU retirement\nrebuilds the selected owner at its stable identity with exact geometry/paint.\nAbove-vault source ground and upper relief triangles remain word-exact, while\nintersecting terrain still clears the bore. Original dimensions, doubled rendered\nterrain heights, fixed40\u00b0 lens, unlimited distance and simulation/commands/RNG stay\nunchanged. All32 HQ models remain6/10; zero8/10 approvals exist.\n\nLocal sealed evidence passes native213, baseline assets204, harness94, boundary140\nand22 quiet native render/save controls, including640 exact selected-owner cache\nrebuild views, eight unchanged source/world comparisons, complete original fallback,\nand real tunnel-ground capture at zooms0/4/5. Ordinary costed freight plus passenger/\nmail operations reach180, and both backends actually render the saved temperate\nsize1 HQ with four ground owners and no invented bodies. Neither a rating proxy nor\na diagnostic layout is substituted for that world-state evidence.\n\nThe**84 larger HQ prototypes are excluded**. Their source-guided medium-east wall\nrepair is still under individual review; correct compound union or structural\ntests do not approve each owner. Source fidelity across every model/state/climate,\nlocks/rivers/disasters, fleet/emitter clearance, strict backend consistency,\nWindows ARM64 execution/GPU/input and replay/network remain unfinished.\nTwo600-frame controls retain136/132 intervals over20ms, a50.356959ms OpenGL work\nstall and2.86/3.07GB sampled peaks: no sustained smooth60fps/memory acceptance.\n\nPortable verification:`opentt3d/reviews/20261003/hq-runtime-repair/verification.json`.\nCatalogue SHA-256:\n`6e5be58e30a55d36be9d1e40a118739fc687d3a84afa22ebf3217469350ca56d`.\nPackages must bundle OpenGFX2 Classic and retain the existing Windows x64/x86/ARM64,\nmacOS Apple silicon/Intel15+ and Linux x86-64/glibc2.36/GCC12 platform limits.\nPublication must change only the audited draft flag, without rebuilding bytes.\n",
