      "body": "# First two original HQ sizes \u2014 `.41` withheld\n\n**Do not publish or recommend this immutable candidate.** Subsequent independent\nowner-LOD analysis found that ordinary coarse-block aggregation can inflate the\ndisjoint HQ source owners into shared blocks: the two-cell factor already shares\n11/15 blocks for ordinary tiny/small HQs and24/76 for Toyland, reaching four owners\nper block. Larger factors remain rejected too. The tag stays unchanged, all draft\nattachments/failures are retained, and the recommended public download stays`.40`.\nAn occupancy-preserving automatic LOD repair is being validated separately; it\nmust not be substituted into this tag's packages or treated as an existing pass.\n\nEvidence:`build-macos/breadth-original-hq-independent-lod-inflation-rejection.json`.\nThe first two-size local checks below predate that expanded LOD analysis.\n\nThis is a development checkpoint, not completion of the every-model8/10 goal.\nDesktop packages remain gated on all eight packaging jobs and independent\nexact-tag audits. The audited public`.40`remains the recommended download until\nthose gates pass; no candidate package is recommended in advance.\n\n## What changed\n\n- 32 genuine independently owned XYZ ground models recreate original HQ sizes0/1\n  in four climates, including ordinary cottage/shed/fence and Toyland turret,\n  flag, checker courtyard and castellated walls.\n- Source-owner planes retain the coherent north structure without changing the\n  disjoint joined compound, four-tile footprint or intentionally absent bodies.\n- The small ordinary fence is inset to its source scale and keeps the path open.\n  A diagnostic coplanar support floor is corrected without changing runtime art.\n- Original placement/upgrade thresholds, commands, simulation RNG, company colours\n  and complete-family fallback remain unchanged. All1,799 earlier models/material\n  faces/definitions/bindings are retained exactly in the1,831-model catalogue.\n\n## Local validation and quality\n\nNative211, asset204, harness94 and presentation-boundary140 pass. Eight final\nhidden climate/backend geometry/atlas/picking/synchronous-save controls pass.\nRemoving one owner preserves all37 original source layers and the entire screenshot\nexactly on both backends. All34 native studies are backend-identical; individual,\njoined and original source studies remain exact after the diagnostic-floor fix.\n\nThirty-two HQ models are individually rated6/10, with40 portable owner/joined\nsource/eight-view sheets and eight natural size0 world captures. The2,494-entry\nledger has57 individual reviews and zero8/10 approvals; required-eight fails.\nWider strict comparisons retain31/31/31/28 differing views and1,001/1,001/1,001/965\npixels, plus10/9/12/8 world pixels. Source detail, natural size1 upgrades, independent\nowner LOD transitions and wider rendering consistency remain unaccepted.\n\nTwo600-frame controls pass their technical gates but retain pacing stalls; neither\naverage frame rate nor small-scene workload grants sustained arbitrary-world60fps.\nLarger HQ sizes2\u20264, locks/rivers/disasters, full fleet clearance, emitter contexts,\ncatalogue-wide individual fidelity, long-duration memory, Windows ARM64 execution/\nGPU/foreground input and replay/network acceptance remain open.\n\nOriginals, rejected column/shrink/paint studies, CLI/exporter and coplanar-floor\nfailures remain preserved. Do not move failed tags or replace audited attachments.\nPackages must bundle OpenGFX2 Classic and retain the existing Windows x64/x86/ARM64,\nmacOS Apple silicon/Intel15+ and Linux x86-64/glibc2.36/GCC12 platform limits.\n",
